1
00:02:31,068 --> 00:02:41,068
All pirates searching for the treasure One Piece must brave the second half of the Grand Line.

2
00:02:41,068 --> 00:02:45,068
These wild and dangerous seas are known as the New World.

3
00:02:45,068 --> 00:02:52,068
Gold Roger and his crew were the only men to ever chart these waters and learn all the secrets they held.

4
00:02:52,068 --> 00:02:59,068
For the rest of the pirates of the world, this has proven to be the end of the road, a graveyard of dreams.

5
00:02:59,068 --> 00:03:09,068
Now, Monkey D. Luffy, a boy whose body became rubber after eating the gum gum fruit, sets sail into the New World with his faithful crew.

6
00:03:09,068 --> 00:03:13,068
I'm gonna be the king of the pirates!

7
00:03:15,068 --> 00:03:23,068
During their journey to the New World, Luffy and his crew arrive on Fishman Island, which is located 10,000 meters below sea level.

8
00:03:23,068 --> 00:03:32,068
There, they found themselves facing the New Fishman Pirates, who were looking to destroy the Ryugu Kingdom and instigated an all-out war.

9
00:03:32,068 --> 00:03:41,068
After a long and grueling battle, Luffy finally defeated Hordy, the captain of the New Fishman Pirates, thwarting their plan for revenge.

10
00:03:41,068 --> 00:03:48,068
Two years ago, up in Shandora, I read a poneglyph that located one of the ancient weapons.

11
00:03:48,068 --> 00:03:53,068
This mermaid princess who lived during the same time as Joy Boy.

12
00:03:53,068 --> 00:03:56,068
She was known by another name as well, wasn't she?

13
00:03:56,068 --> 00:03:57,068
Wasn't she?

14
00:03:57,068 --> 00:03:59,068
She is the ancient weapon.

15
00:03:59,068 --> 00:04:01,068
Poseidon!

16
00:04:05,068 --> 00:04:07,068
The Straw Hat stunned!

17
00:04:07,068 --> 00:04:09,068
The new Fleet Admiral of the Navy!

18
00:04:09,068 --> 00:04:34,068
Many years ago, for some unknown purpose, there were three powerful entities that could destroy this entire world.

19
00:04:34,068 --> 00:04:43,068
They were ancient weapons named after gods. Pluton, Uranus, and Poseidon.

20
00:04:44,068 --> 00:04:47,068
And one of those great weapons is… the princess.

21
00:04:48,068 --> 00:04:49,068
Indeed.

22
00:04:51,068 --> 00:04:55,068
Well, if that's the case, we can't let anyone else know about this.

23
00:04:56,068 --> 00:05:02,068
If we did, the government and every other organization would want Shirahoshi for themselves, not to mention other pirates.

24
00:05:04,068 --> 00:05:10,068
Ancient weapons? Strong enough to destroy the whole world?

25
00:05:15,068 --> 00:05:19,068
To think I was just going to take off after stealing all their silly trinkets!

26
00:05:19,068 --> 00:05:23,068
How foolish of me! I almost overlooked the most valuable item they've got!

27
00:05:24,068 --> 00:05:27,068
That mermaid princess is more precious than I imagined!

28
00:05:27,068 --> 00:05:30,068
Yee-haw!

29
00:05:35,068 --> 00:05:37,068
Whew! I think I can go for another plate!

30
00:05:37,068 --> 00:05:39,068
Don't tell me you've scarfed down that much food already!

31
00:05:39,068 --> 00:05:43,068
Can you blame me? It's all so good! I can eat this stuff until I die!

32
00:05:43,068 --> 00:05:44,068
Especially the candy!

33
00:05:47,068 --> 00:05:50,068
It's as good as meat! I'll take a hundred more!

34
00:05:50,068 --> 00:05:54,068
Wh-well, actually, I'm afraid we've just about run out of the candy!

35
00:05:54,068 --> 00:05:57,068
But I'd be happy to bring you something else to eat if you'd like me to!

36
00:06:00,068 --> 00:06:01,068
Okay, sure!

37
00:06:05,068 --> 00:06:06,068
Tell me something, Luffy!

38
00:06:07,068 --> 00:06:08,068
Why you sit here stuffing your face?

39
00:06:08,068 --> 00:06:10,068
Are you aware of all that's been happening in the world?

40
00:06:11,068 --> 00:06:13,068
Huh? What are you getting at, Jinbei?

41
00:06:13,068 --> 00:06:15,068
Ah, so you're completely uninformed!

42
00:06:16,068 --> 00:06:18,068
That's a problem, but I can't say I'm shocked!

43
00:06:19,068 --> 00:06:20,068
I'm lost!

44
00:06:22,068 --> 00:06:23,068
We brought you more food, Luffy!

45
00:06:24,068 --> 00:06:25,068
Come with me!

46
00:06:26,068 --> 00:06:28,068
Sure! Just give me a second!

47
00:06:31,068 --> 00:06:32,068
I'm gonna take this one to go!

48
00:06:43,068 --> 00:06:44,068
Hey!

49
00:06:44,068 --> 00:06:45,068
Hmm?

50
00:06:45,068 --> 00:06:46,068
You guys left the party, too?

51
00:06:49,068 --> 00:06:50,068
I'm trying to sober up.

52
00:06:50,068 --> 00:06:51,068
I drank too much.

53
00:06:52,068 --> 00:06:53,068
And I ate too much!

54
00:06:54,068 --> 00:06:55,068
Sanji flirted too much!

55
00:06:56,068 --> 00:06:58,068
This place is so magical!

56
00:06:58,068 --> 00:06:59,068
There's so many babes!

57
00:06:59,068 --> 00:07:00,068
I can't take it!

58
00:07:02,068 --> 00:07:03,068
What?!

59
00:07:03,068 --> 00:07:05,068
Chilaka, Inu, and Aokiji fought each other?!

60
00:07:06,068 --> 00:07:07,068
It was a major event!

61
00:07:08,068 --> 00:07:11,068
Did Rayleigh never mention this to you during your training?

62
00:07:11,068 --> 00:07:12,068
Nope!

63
00:07:12,068 --> 00:07:13,068
This is news to me!

64
00:07:14,068 --> 00:07:15,068
That was cruel of him!

65
00:07:16,068 --> 00:07:18,068
Oh, I knew about it the whole time!

66
00:07:18,068 --> 00:07:19,068
So did I do good?!

67
00:07:19,068 --> 00:07:20,068
That's crazy!

68
00:07:24,068 --> 00:07:27,068
It all started two years ago, right after the war ended.

69
00:07:28,068 --> 00:07:30,068
Sengoku resigned as Fleet Admiral.

70
00:07:32,068 --> 00:07:38,068
Aokiji was well-liked among his own men, so Sengoku nominated him to take over the title.

71
00:07:39,068 --> 00:07:44,068
But many high-ranking officials favored Aka Inu, so he became a contender as well.

72
00:07:47,068 --> 00:07:52,068
Aokiji is normally cool-tempered, but he was quite adamant in his disapproval of Aka Inu.

73
00:07:53,068 --> 00:07:55,068
He found him unfit for the position.

74
00:07:55,068 --> 00:08:00,068
So it did not take long for the disagreement to come to blows on an island somewhere.

75
00:08:01,068 --> 00:08:04,068
It was the first and final battle between the two admirals.

76
00:08:07,068 --> 00:08:12,068
It was agreed that whoever lost would withdraw his candidacy without protest.

77
00:08:13,068 --> 00:08:17,068
And the winner would become the leader of the Navy.

78
00:08:17,068 --> 00:08:23,068
As the rest of the world now knows, they fought for ten whole days.

79
00:08:24,068 --> 00:08:26,068
The two opponents were equally matched in power.

80
00:08:27,068 --> 00:08:29,068
But the duel finally ended.

81
00:08:30,068 --> 00:08:35,068
Aka Inu, or as some know him, Sakazuki, emerged victorious.

82
00:08:37,068 --> 00:08:38,068
That bastard won!

83
00:08:38,068 --> 00:08:41,068
I'm putting an end to this!

84
00:08:48,068 --> 00:08:50,068
So did he kill Aokiji?

85
00:08:51,068 --> 00:08:52,068
Well, both admirals were severely injured.

86
00:08:53,068 --> 00:08:56,068
In fact, Aokiji couldn't even stand after it was over.

87
00:08:57,068 --> 00:08:59,068
However, Aka Inu was strangely merciful towards him.

88
00:09:00,068 --> 00:09:02,068
Despite this, Aokiji refused to accept the result.

89
00:09:03,068 --> 00:09:05,068
He has resigned from the Navy.

90
00:09:06,068 --> 00:09:08,068
I can't believe Aokiji would just up and quit like that.

91
00:09:09,068 --> 00:09:10,068
Indeed.

92
00:09:11,068 --> 00:09:13,068
I wonder what's been going through his mind since then.

93
00:09:14,068 --> 00:09:17,068
The government has certainly lost a valuable asset.

94
00:09:19,068 --> 00:09:20,068
You can say that again.

95
00:09:21,068 --> 00:09:24,068
The admirals were the main reason the Navy was so powerful, weren't they?

96
00:09:25,068 --> 00:09:26,068
At first, yes.

97
00:09:26,068 --> 00:09:29,068
But they have found ways to overcompensate in Aokiji's absence.

98
00:09:29,068 --> 00:09:32,068
One might argue that they're more dangerous than ever now.

99
00:09:39,068 --> 00:09:40,068
There is still much you do not know.

100
00:09:41,068 --> 00:09:42,068
Listen closely.

101
00:09:42,068 --> 00:09:43,068
Before you reach the New World,

102
00:09:44,068 --> 00:09:47,068
you must be aware of two key changes that have occurred there.

103
00:09:49,068 --> 00:09:52,068
Now then, the first matter, as I've already begun to explain,

104
00:09:53,068 --> 00:09:56,068
is that the Navy under Fleet Admiral Sakazuki is stronger than before.

105
00:09:56,068 --> 00:10:02,068
And secondly, the Blackbeard Pirates are making strides of their own.

106
00:10:03,068 --> 00:10:04,068
Those guys again?

107
00:10:05,068 --> 00:10:06,068
You mean the ones we met back in Mocktown?

108
00:10:07,068 --> 00:10:09,068
They attacked my homeland. I can never forget them.

109
00:10:09,068 --> 00:10:10,068
I can never forget them.

110
00:10:12,068 --> 00:10:16,068
This new era they keep rambling on and on about is a load of crap.

111
00:10:17,068 --> 00:10:20,068
The era when pirates dream of treasure will come to an end?

112
00:10:21,068 --> 00:10:22,068
Right!

113
00:10:22,068 --> 00:10:23,068
What are you talking about?

114
00:10:23,068 --> 00:10:36,068
The dreams of pirates will never end!

115
00:10:37,068 --> 00:10:38,068
So you're...

116
00:10:39,068 --> 00:10:40,068
Blackbeard!

117
00:10:41,068 --> 00:10:42,068
Huh?

118
00:10:42,068 --> 00:10:44,068
Oh, right. I guess I never gave you my name, did I?

119
00:10:44,068 --> 00:10:49,068
Z-hahaha! Long time no see, Straw Hat Luffy!

120
00:10:50,068 --> 00:10:54,068
He spent many years as a member of the Whitebeard Pirates.

121
00:10:55,068 --> 00:10:57,068
He was already familiar with the territory,

122
00:10:58,068 --> 00:10:59,068
so after their captain died,

123
00:11:00,068 --> 00:11:03,068
Blackbeard wasted no time in seizing control of it for himself.

124
00:11:03,068 --> 00:11:07,068
Using the Tremor Tremor fruit he stole upon Whitebeard's death.

125
00:11:08,068 --> 00:11:16,068
He's gaining quite the reputation, along with Shanks, Kaido, and Big Mom.

126
00:11:17,068 --> 00:11:20,068
He's joined the ranks of the Four Emperors.

127
00:11:21,068 --> 00:11:26,068
So he stole Whitebeard's devil fruit and his title? Talk about a scumbag!

128
00:11:27,068 --> 00:11:29,068
I agree, his audacity is infuriating.

129
00:11:29,068 --> 00:11:34,068
There's a rumor going around that they're currently on the hunt for those with devil fruit powers.

130
00:11:35,068 --> 00:11:41,068
I am not sure how it's possible, but it seems they found a way to acquire abilities from the other people upon killing them.

131
00:11:42,068 --> 00:11:46,068
Clearly they plan to usurp the strongest powers they can find and become unstoppable.

132
00:11:47,068 --> 00:11:48,068
Be on your guard!

133
00:11:49,068 --> 00:11:52,068
No, they're gonna take mine!

134
00:11:53,068 --> 00:11:54,068
The human-human fruit? I think you're safe.

135
00:11:55,068 --> 00:11:56,068
You sure?

136
00:11:56,068 --> 00:11:59,068
I worry for you the most, Luffy.

137
00:12:00,068 --> 00:12:04,068
I know there's a great deal of bad blood between you and Teach.

138
00:12:05,068 --> 00:12:06,068
You must take care.

139
00:12:13,068 --> 00:12:14,068
Luffy!

140
00:12:15,068 --> 00:12:16,068
Have you been listening to me?

141
00:12:16,068 --> 00:12:17,068
Huh?

142
00:12:17,068 --> 00:12:18,068
You're supposed to be the captain here!

143
00:12:19,068 --> 00:12:22,068
The captain needs to have at least some idea of the situation!

144
00:12:23,068 --> 00:12:26,068
Whoa. It's okay, Jinbei. The rest of us heard you.

145
00:12:27,068 --> 00:12:30,068
Huh? I thought the captain was supposed to goof off while the crew looks out for him!

146
00:12:31,068 --> 00:12:36,068
Shame on you, Luffy! A good captain dedicates his life to the safety of his crew, and here you are-

147
00:12:36,068 --> 00:12:41,068
Don't be such a drag! I'd rather take my chances and see what happens! It's more fun that way!

148
00:12:46,068 --> 00:12:48,068
I don't envy you all one bit!

149
00:12:49,068 --> 00:12:50,068
Tell me about it!

150
00:12:51,068 --> 00:12:52,068
Are you here, Luffy-chan?

151
00:12:53,068 --> 00:12:57,068
There you are! The party's for you, you know! Why are all you guys hiding out?

152
00:12:57,068 --> 00:12:58,068
Hey, Kami!

153
00:12:59,068 --> 00:13:02,068
Oh, yeah. What happened to Weepy Hoshi? Did she leave?

154
00:13:03,068 --> 00:13:07,068
She was tired. All the excitement made her need a little nap, so she went up to her room.

155
00:13:16,068 --> 00:13:19,068
Hang on. Zoro? Sanji?

156
00:13:20,068 --> 00:13:24,068
It seems like there's some kind of monster here.

157
00:13:24,068 --> 00:13:28,068
You may be right. Yeah, I feel it too.

158
00:13:33,068 --> 00:13:41,068
I never dreamed a party could be such fun. I might have to take a little nap just to recover from it all.

159
00:13:41,068 --> 00:13:43,068
Have you ever been playing aroundre Chief-a?

160
00:13:44,068 --> 00:13:45,068
Ah!

161
00:13:49,068 --> 00:13:50,068
Are you…

162
00:13:51,068 --> 00:13:53,068
It looks like there's no time to take care of the rest of the ship!

163
00:13:54,068 --> 00:13:55,068
Well, it's possible that he wants to go to our new ship...

164
00:13:56,068 --> 00:13:58,068
Eh.

165
00:14:03,068 --> 00:14:05,068
Are you unaf fights against you?

166
00:14:05,068 --> 00:14:05,708
Bah!

167
00:14:06,128 --> 00:14:07,208
Ah!

168
00:14:07,408 --> 00:14:08,268
Ah!

169
00:14:08,648 --> 00:14:13,168
Ah!

170
00:14:13,168 --> 00:14:14,108
Ah!

171
00:14:15,308 --> 00:14:21,308
Ha, ha, ha, ha, haa!

172
00:14:21,308 --> 00:14:21,888
Ya!

173
00:14:21,888 --> 00:14:27,048
Ah, ha, ha, ha, ha, ha!

174
00:14:27,228 --> 00:14:29,128
The Mets

175
00:14:35,068 --> 00:14:37,068
The End

176
00:14:37,068 --> 00:14:39,068
The End

177
00:14:39,068 --> 00:14:41,068
The End

178
00:14:41,068 --> 00:14:43,068
The End

179
00:14:43,068 --> 00:14:45,068
Help me!

180
00:14:45,068 --> 00:14:47,068
Shhh!

181
00:14:47,068 --> 00:14:51,068
Oh, you please! I can't even help me!

182
00:14:51,068 --> 00:14:53,068
Help me!

183
00:14:53,068 --> 00:14:55,068
Help me!

184
00:14:55,068 --> 00:14:57,068
Help me!

185
00:14:57,068 --> 00:14:59,068
Help me!

186
00:14:59,068 --> 00:15:01,068
Help me!

187
00:15:01,068 --> 00:15:03,068
You cut me to the quick, princess!

188
00:15:03,068 --> 00:15:07,068
Don't look so unhappy to see me!

189
00:15:07,068 --> 00:15:09,068
Just relax.

190
00:15:09,068 --> 00:15:11,068
I promise I won't do anything to cause you pain,

191
00:15:11,068 --> 00:15:13,068
my dear.

192
00:15:13,068 --> 00:15:15,068
I was ready to settle for just the treasure

193
00:15:15,068 --> 00:15:17,068
after selling off the other mermaids turned out

194
00:15:17,068 --> 00:15:19,068
to be a hassle, but you might just be

195
00:15:19,068 --> 00:15:21,068
an exception!

196
00:15:21,068 --> 00:15:23,068
Now then, I want you to be a good girl and go to sleep

197
00:15:23,068 --> 00:15:25,068
for a little while. Can you do that for me?

198
00:15:25,068 --> 00:15:27,068
I just received word from my brother.

199
00:15:27,068 --> 00:15:29,068
He and the crew have made port on

200
00:15:29,068 --> 00:15:31,068
Fishman Island. We're all headed

201
00:15:31,068 --> 00:15:33,068
into the new world and we'd like

202
00:15:33,068 --> 00:15:35,068
for you to come along with us!

203
00:15:35,068 --> 00:15:37,068
Zuh!

204
00:15:37,068 --> 00:15:39,068
Now now. Show me a smile!

205
00:15:39,068 --> 00:15:41,068
He he he he he he

206
00:15:41,068 --> 00:15:43,068
He he he he he he he he he!

207
00:15:43,068 --> 00:15:45,068
You! Oh what do you want, Straw Hat?

208
00:15:45,068 --> 00:15:47,068
Go find your own mermaid princess.

209
00:15:47,068 --> 00:15:49,068
We're busy!

210
00:15:49,068 --> 00:15:52,288
Rafi!

211
00:16:00,228 --> 00:16:02,068
King!

212
00:16:02,488 --> 00:16:03,568
It's you!

213
00:16:04,488 --> 00:16:05,208
Wolfie!

214
00:16:10,768 --> 00:16:11,528
Oh!

215
00:16:14,668 --> 00:16:15,988
That guy was still here.

216
00:16:17,048 --> 00:16:17,608
Wolfie!

217
00:16:17,608 --> 00:16:22,608
That was scary! Thank you for saving me!

218
00:16:22,608 --> 00:16:27,608
Luffy, you lucky bastard! I should have kicked him while I had the chance!

219
00:16:27,608 --> 00:16:30,608
Wasn't that the pirate we captured not too long ago?

220
00:16:30,608 --> 00:16:34,608
I haven't seen him since we left the island. Hell, I haven't even thought about him.

221
00:16:34,608 --> 00:16:36,608
Oh well, I guess he's gone now.

222
00:16:36,608 --> 00:16:40,608
That was a close call. We really can't thank you enough, Luffy.

223
00:16:40,608 --> 00:16:41,608
It's no big deal.

224
00:16:41,608 --> 00:16:45,608
That ruffian who stole from us! I can't believe he was still nearby!

225
00:16:45,608 --> 00:16:49,608
This place is usually locked up so tight even a guppy can't get in.

226
00:16:49,608 --> 00:16:52,608
But with everything that's happened, it seems we left it open.

227
00:16:52,608 --> 00:16:56,608
And look! That big tower over there has been sliced clean in two!

228
00:16:56,608 --> 00:16:59,608
The robber must have done it while we were out in the plaza!

229
00:17:01,608 --> 00:17:05,608
Sorry, actually that would be this guy. Man, you should have seen him.

230
00:17:05,608 --> 00:17:08,608
When they got out of the cage, he was hacking and slashing all over the block!

231
00:17:08,608 --> 00:17:11,608
Please, learn to keep your mouth shut, stupid starfish!

232
00:17:11,608 --> 00:17:14,608
I don't think so! If I don't say something, that makes me an accomplice!

233
00:17:14,608 --> 00:17:18,608
Hey, righty, here's a question.

234
00:17:18,608 --> 00:17:19,608
Righty?

235
00:17:19,608 --> 00:17:21,608
You mentioned a treasure thief, right?

236
00:17:21,608 --> 00:17:26,608
Yes, you heard correctly. That unsavory man who was just here snuck into the palace and robbed us blind.

237
00:17:26,608 --> 00:17:28,608
Really? Well then...

238
00:17:28,608 --> 00:17:30,608
Here we go again!

239
00:17:30,608 --> 00:17:33,608
You're gonna let him steal national treasures?

240
00:17:33,608 --> 00:17:37,608
Now that my people are safe from harm, I care nothing for material riches.

241
00:17:37,608 --> 00:17:39,608
Oh, cut the crap!

242
00:17:39,608 --> 00:17:42,608
Wait, so you're saying you don't want them anymore?

243
00:17:42,608 --> 00:17:47,608
If you can rescue them, you're free to keep them. It's the least I can do for our heroes.

244
00:17:47,608 --> 00:17:49,608
Well, if you insist!

245
00:17:49,608 --> 00:17:50,608
Ugh!

246
00:17:50,608 --> 00:17:55,608
You idiots just had to kick him into next week, didn't you? Why couldn't you just knock him out and tie him up in the tower?

247
00:17:55,608 --> 00:17:58,608
Oh, Nami, you're so cute!

248
00:17:58,608 --> 00:18:01,608
Go catch him and bring him back!

249
00:18:01,608 --> 00:18:03,608
Get back!

250
00:18:07,608 --> 00:18:08,608
Your Majesty!

251
00:18:08,608 --> 00:18:09,608
Hmm?

252
00:18:09,608 --> 00:18:12,608
It's Hordy and his men, sir! Their handcuffs came off!

253
00:18:12,608 --> 00:18:13,608
But how?

254
00:18:13,608 --> 00:18:14,608
Ho!

255
00:18:20,608 --> 00:18:22,608
Damn you humans!

256
00:18:22,608 --> 00:18:24,608
Don't think we've forgotten our grudge!

257
00:18:24,608 --> 00:18:27,608
We'll exact our revenge soon enough!

258
00:18:30,608 --> 00:18:32,608
Then Storhead'll be the first to die!

259
00:18:32,608 --> 00:18:34,608
Bring him to my cell!

260
00:18:34,608 --> 00:18:56,608
Oh, my back hurts! I sure could use a drink!

261
00:18:56,608 --> 00:19:01,608
I aged myself on purpose!

262
00:19:01,608 --> 00:19:06,608
I want to get back at the Straw Hats, but my energy's at an old time low soon!

263
00:19:11,608 --> 00:19:14,608
We won't show them an ounce of mercy!

264
00:19:15,608 --> 00:19:17,608
What in the world has happened here?

265
00:19:17,608 --> 00:19:18,608
Don't tell me!

266
00:19:18,608 --> 00:19:20,608
Is that Hordy and his crew?

267
00:19:21,608 --> 00:19:24,608
You think these guys can hold me?

268
00:19:24,608 --> 00:19:25,608
What a bunch of morons!

269
00:19:27,608 --> 00:19:29,608
I'll break them and...

270
00:19:31,608 --> 00:19:36,608
Captain Hordy!

271
00:19:39,608 --> 00:19:41,608
Why are they so brittle?

272
00:19:41,608 --> 00:19:42,608
Just as I thought!

273
00:19:42,608 --> 00:19:45,608
That energy steroid you were taking to make yourself stronger!

274
00:19:45,608 --> 00:19:48,608
And the pill from inside the Tamate Box!

275
00:19:48,608 --> 00:19:50,608
They're one and the same, aren't they?

276
00:19:50,608 --> 00:19:51,608
A Tamate Box?

277
00:19:51,608 --> 00:19:55,608
A priceless artifact passed down for generations, Jamal!

278
00:19:55,608 --> 00:19:59,608
The pills hidden inside were highly valuable as well!

279
00:19:59,608 --> 00:20:02,608
But ten years ago someone stole them from us!

280
00:20:03,608 --> 00:20:04,608
We failed to catch the culprit!

281
00:20:04,608 --> 00:20:09,608
His Majesty was concerned that a scandal might break out, so we closed the case!

282
00:20:09,608 --> 00:20:14,608
Actually, Hordy, I think that happened around the same time you left the army!

283
00:20:14,608 --> 00:20:16,608
Interesting!

284
00:20:19,608 --> 00:20:21,608
Of course it was me!

285
00:20:21,608 --> 00:20:23,608
Look what's happened to my body!

286
00:20:23,608 --> 00:20:25,608
Need me to spill it out for you!

287
00:20:25,608 --> 00:20:27,608
The pills were treasured heirloans.

288
00:20:27,608 --> 00:20:30,608
The truth behind their purpose lost long ago.

289
00:20:30,608 --> 00:20:35,608
Tales of their power and the curse that accompanied them were both passed down merely as legend.

290
00:20:35,608 --> 00:20:38,608
But still, enough to make us wary.

291
00:20:39,608 --> 00:20:42,608
It would appear that our discretion was warranted, however.

292
00:20:42,608 --> 00:20:46,608
The Tamate Box was carefully guarded for the safety of our people.

293
00:20:46,608 --> 00:20:49,608
This result is truly regrettable.

294
00:20:50,608 --> 00:20:54,608
If you had not allowed your judgment to be clouded by foolish dreams of power,

295
00:20:54,608 --> 00:20:57,608
you would not have subjected yourselves to this terrible fate.

296
00:20:59,608 --> 00:21:01,608
What the hell do you know?

297
00:21:01,608 --> 00:21:08,608
In any case, they'll never get their vengeance now.

298
00:21:11,608 --> 00:21:12,608
You'll see!

299
00:21:12,608 --> 00:21:16,608
The heavens have chosen us to settle the score, and that's just what we'll do!

300
00:21:17,608 --> 00:21:19,608
And we'll not only wipe out the human race,

301
00:21:20,608 --> 00:21:23,608
we'll annihilate you and your entire family!

302
00:21:25,608 --> 00:21:26,608
I pity them.

303
00:21:26,608 --> 00:21:28,608
Perhaps I ought to offer them clemency.

304
00:21:28,608 --> 00:21:31,608
Wait, Captain!

305
00:21:34,608 --> 00:21:37,608
Fukumoshi, you're a disgrace to our people!

306
00:21:43,608 --> 00:21:45,608
Fishman Island is healing now.

307
00:21:45,608 --> 00:21:49,608
So although you killed my mother, I will not hold a grudge.

308
00:21:51,608 --> 00:21:55,608
The least that you can do is refrain from speaking.

309
00:21:56,608 --> 00:21:59,608
I don't want the children hearing your poisonous words.

310
00:22:08,608 --> 00:22:10,608
Minister of the Left!

311
00:22:10,608 --> 00:22:11,608
Huh?

312
00:22:11,608 --> 00:22:12,608
Baron Tamago!

313
00:22:12,608 --> 00:22:13,608
And Mr. Peikums!

314
00:22:13,608 --> 00:22:15,608
They're at the Sweets Factory!

315
00:22:16,608 --> 00:22:18,608
They're here to collect for Big Mom.

316
00:22:18,608 --> 00:22:20,608
We can't face them now.

317
00:22:21,608 --> 00:22:23,608
Hand over the Sweets!

318
00:22:24,608 --> 00:22:25,608
Gah!

319
00:22:28,608 --> 00:22:30,608
Don't keep Mama waiting.

320
00:22:31,608 --> 00:22:32,608
Toot Sweet.

321
00:22:37,608 --> 00:22:39,608
We don't have any sweets for this month's payment!

322
00:22:40,608 --> 00:22:42,608
Hordy and his lackeys tore the factory apart!

323
00:22:42,608 --> 00:22:47,608
And all the candy we could salvage was sent to the banquet so the Straw Hats could enjoy it!

324
00:22:47,608 --> 00:22:48,608
What should we do?

325
00:22:53,608 --> 00:22:59,608
Something tells me Big Mom of the Four Emperors won't be satisfied with an apology.

326
00:22:59,608 --> 00:23:04,608
That woman would level an entire country for sweets!

327
00:23:07,608 --> 00:23:13,608
While the Straw Hats rush to retrieve Fishman Island's stolen treasure, pirates working for Big Mom appear.

328
00:23:14,608 --> 00:23:19,608
After scarcely avoiding destruction at Hordy's hand, the island is now under threat from an even stronger adversary.

329
00:23:19,608 --> 00:23:26,608
Luffy steps up to save the Fishman once again, but may doom himself by antagonizing one of the strongest pirates in the New World.

330
00:23:27,608 --> 00:23:28,608
On the next, One Piece!

331
00:23:29,608 --> 00:23:30,608
She loves sweets!

332
00:23:31,608 --> 00:23:32,608
Big Mom of the Four Emperors!

333
00:23:33,608 --> 00:23:34,608
I'm gonna be King of the Pirates!

